2781938,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cVHny","user":{"login":"tracefree","id":155747722,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUiFig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155747722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree","html_url":"https://github.com/tracefree","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-29T20:32:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-29T20:32:28Z","body":"Hi! Is there anything blocking this PR or is it planned for merging in the 4.5 development cycle? If it helps I could test it in my project.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2622781938/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624999789","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98287#issuecomment-2624999789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98287","id":2624999789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cdlFt","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T16:38:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T16:38:20Z","body":"> Tested locally, I found a crash.\r\n\r\nAdded few extra checks to prevent crash on reading from empty `mem` file.\r\n\r\nNote: test code is non-functional, `mem` files exist only if there's reference to the file and the only write reference is closed before reading:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n...\r\n\r\nprint(\"Beginning write of %s://test.bin (200 MB).\" % PREFIX)\r\nvar file_large = method.call(\"%s://test.bin\" % PREFIX, FileAccess.WRITE)\r\nfor i in 50_000_000:\r\n\tfile_large.store_32(0)\r\nprint(\"Done writing 1 GB to memory.\")\r\nfile_large.close() # <-------- mem file is deleted here.\r\n\r\nprint(\"Beginning read of %s://test.bin.\" % PREFIX)\r\nvar read_large = method.call(\"%s://test.bin\" % PREFIX, FileAccess.READ) # <-------- completly new, empty mem file created.\r\nprint(read_large.get_32())\r\nread_large.seek(200_000_000)\r\nprint(read_large.get_32())\r\nprint(\"Done reading %s://test.bin.\" % PREFIX)\r\nread_large.close()\r\n\r\n...\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624999789/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629273183","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98287#issuecomment-2629273183","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98287","id":2629273183,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ct4Zf","user":{"login":"tracefree","id":155747722,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUiFig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155747722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree","html_url":"https://github.com/tracefree","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tracefree/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T07:02:23Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T07:02:23Z","body":"I tested it and it works great, thank you! One thing that doesn't work, likely because it is out of scope for this PR, is directory access. I can create files in \"directories\" with `FileAccess.open(\"mem://dir/file.txt\")`, but I can't do `DirAccess.get_files_at(\"mem://dir/\")` or copy with `DirAccess.copy_absolute(local_file, \"mem://file.txt\")`, they just return errors. Do you think support for these operations could feasibly be added in a future PR? And/or would it be possible to provide an option to keep files in memory when the last reference goes out of scope, and let them be freed later with `DirAccess.remove_absolute` for example?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629273183/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2932408321","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98287#issuecomment-2932408321","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98287","id":2932408321,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uyQAB","user":{"login":"PiCode9560","id":122909224,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1NyKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122909224?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560","html_url":"https://github.com/PiCode9560","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-02T20:39:46Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T20:39:46Z","body":"I found a bug. With this setup, it prints \"file exist: true\" only for 2 seconds, then it turns to false. Without the timer, it is instantly false.\r\n```\r\nextends Node3D\r\n\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\t\r\n\tvar load_file = FileAccess.open(\"res://new_box_mesh.tres\", FileAccess.READ)\r\n\tvar content = load_file.get_as_text()\r\n\r\n\tvar file = FileAccess.open(\"mem://new_box_mesh.tres\", FileAccess.WRITE)\r\n\tfile.store_string(content)\r\n\r\n\tawait get_tree().create_timer(2).timeout\r\n\r\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\r\n\tprint(\"FILE EXIST: \",FileAccess.file_exists(\"mem://new_box_mesh.tres\"))\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2932408321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2932428038","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98287#issuecomment-2932428038","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98287","id":2932428038,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uyU0G","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-02T20:45:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T20:45:05Z","body":"> I found a bug. \r\n\r\nThis is expected behavior, memory file is freed when the last `FileAccess` reference to the file is removed, `await` is the only thing keeping the local re